summary:
  The helper is handed the stream's address as an argument.

history:
  An argv is readable by every user on the machine for as long as the
  process lives, here for twenty seconds, and an address can carry a
  listener's token.

target:
  package/contents/ui/LoudLogic.js

find:
  python3 -B " + q(a.scriptPath) + " " + q(a.urlPath) + " " + LISTEN_S

replace:
  python3 -B " + q(a.scriptPath) + " " + q(a.url) + " " + LISTEN_S

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_loudlogic.qml::test_the_address_goes_into_a_file_and_never_to_the_helper.
  Line-neutral.
